{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAQXvmg26q1sGBmZncwf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I changed `Hijack` so it works after the headers have been written, as long as no body bytes have gone out yet. All tests pass, but I couldn't commit because git has no author identity set here.\n\n**The problem:** `Hijack` refused whenever `Written()` was true. That includes the case where only the headers were sent (`size == 0`, no body). WebSocket libraries like `github.com/coder/websocket` send the `101 Switching Protocols` header first and then hijack the connection, so they got an error.\n\n**The change, in `response_writer.go`:**\n- `Hijack` now returns an error only when `w.size > 0`, meaning some body data has been written.\n- It still works before anything is written, and now also after only the headers are written.\n- I added a comment on `Hijack` explaining why, and changed the error message to `\"gin: response body already written\"`.\n\n**Tests, in `response_writer_test.go`:** I added a case to `TestResponseWriterHijackAfterWrite` that writes a 101 status with `WriteHeaderNow()` and then checks that hijacking succeeds. The existing case where hijacking after a body write fails still passes. `go test ./...` passes and `gofmt` reports no issues.\n\nThe changes are on a new branch, `fix/hijack-after-headers`, but not committed. I didn't want to set a git identity for you. Once you've set one with `git config user.name` and `git config user.email`, I can commit with the message I drafted, `fix(response): refine hijack behavior for response lifecycle`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":34457,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":388,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4066a71-517f-4bb7-9d08-7b95e54028af","uuid":"2b8eb2dc-871f-4afc-b760-d8e37696c7a7","timestamp":"2026-10-18T21:23:56.877Z","request_id":"req_011CgAQXvZXCqJn4LvBHAXKs"}
